# 8. VeriMe may be an even bigger signal

This is very new.

**Laure Haak, the founding executive director of ORCID, is now involved in VeriMe Cooperative**, which is working specifically on **verified researcher identity**. It has already partnered with Dryad on researcher identity-verification workflows. ([Publication Ethics][13])

The direction is:

```text
ORCID:
"I claim I am researcher X"

        ↓

VeriMe:
"researcher X's identity has been verified"
```

And its wider concept involves letting researchers connect verified identities to research systems and reputational services. ([VERIME Cooperative][14])

Notice what's happening.

The ecosystem is slowly assembling:

```text
ORCID
identity

VeriMe
verified identity

Crossref/DataCite
objects + provenance

ORKG
structured scholarly knowledge

PREreview
credited expert review

PCI
public expert endorsement

ResearchHub
paid verification
```

Nobody owns the entire stack.

